<CompareLayout
	slug="saas-starter-kits"
	h1="Rocketflare vs ShipFast, Supastarter, Makerkit and SaaS Pegasus"
	lede="Paid SaaS starter kits save you the first month of plumbing, and the good ones are worth the money. They differ from Rocketflare in three places: they include billing and it does not, their AI is an example where Rocketflare’s is a working layer with agents and a knowledge base, and their licences restrict what you can do with the code."
	glance={[
		{ label: 'They include', body: 'Stripe or several payment providers, wired to plans and checkout.' },
		{ label: 'Rocketflare includes', body: 'Durable AI agents with approvals, a knowledge base, evals and cost tracking, OIDC single sign-on, and isolation checked by tests.' },
		{ label: 'The price', body: 'They cost $199 to $1,499 once, with licence conditions. Rocketflare is free under MIT.' },
	]}
	shortAnswer="If you need billing on day one, buy Supastarter (B2B, several payment providers) or ShipFast (consumer, fast checkout). If you are building a B2B product where AI does real work, or you build for clients, start from Rocketflare: it is free and MIT licensed, and its agents, knowledge base and tenancy go further than any paid kit we checked. You add Stripe yourself."
